WEBVTT

00:16.328 --> 00:17.955
Director Evans.

00:18.038 --> 00:20.833
What? Where did you come from?

00:20.916 --> 00:24.545
I'm sorry, sir. I did knock a few times…

00:24.628 --> 00:27.256
Fine, fine… What do you want?

00:28.007 --> 00:32.011
Um… May I go home for the day?

00:34.013 --> 00:37.349
I'm sorry, sir.
I had plans for this evening…

00:37.433 --> 00:41.228
I hadn't realized that managing
your schedule was also my job.

00:41.312 --> 00:44.023
N-No, sir. It's just…

00:44.106 --> 00:47.860
I wanted to celebrate
my son getting into the Academy…

00:47.943 --> 00:52.948
Oh! Well, that's wonderful. We all
look forward to another legacy hire.

00:53.032 --> 00:56.827
Just find someone to fetch the UG2 sample.

00:56.911 --> 01:00.039
Everyone has already
gone home at this hour…

01:02.083 --> 01:05.628
I'll bring over the sample myself… so…

01:05.711 --> 01:10.674
How very kind of you.
Fetch it and get out of my sight.

01:22.853 --> 01:24.522
Director Evans?

01:33.823 --> 01:35.032
Wait…

01:43.541 --> 01:45.417
What happened in there?

01:46.043 --> 01:49.338
Lost you for a sec.
Someone raise a jammer?

01:49.421 --> 01:51.549
Transmission was stable.

01:52.216 --> 01:53.175
Weird.

01:54.844 --> 01:57.972
Yeesh, what a boring gig.

03:32.024 --> 03:36.695
They trespassed on Arasaka premises,
hit us in our own fucking facility.

03:36.779 --> 03:40.950
The lab's research focused
on Militech countermeasures.

03:41.033 --> 03:44.161
Is this related to the runner
who flatlined Jamie and Marcus?

03:44.245 --> 03:46.538
Evans was murdered by a bullet…

03:46.622 --> 03:51.418
This was sloppy, violent.
Safe to say, not the same runner.

03:51.502 --> 03:55.714
Apprehending the netrunner's our priority.
They're too dangerous.

03:55.798 --> 03:58.717
But we know neither
their motive nor purpose…

03:58.801 --> 04:00.886
Whoever they are, they're cautious.

04:00.970 --> 04:03.555
Not your average runner looking to score.

04:03.639 --> 04:06.725
We're Arasaka Counterintel.
We never deal with average.

04:06.809 --> 04:10.062
We'll need to take a detour
to catch the runner's trail.

04:10.145 --> 04:13.148
Are we going after Evans' killer?

04:13.232 --> 04:16.986
It's two separate roads.
We may get lucky and find that they merge.

04:17.820 --> 04:21.532
Let's switch it up.
We'll go after the fixer.

04:21.615 --> 04:25.327
Who do we know that has ties to Militech?

04:25.411 --> 04:29.415
But if the fixer we get
has ties to the runner,

04:29.498 --> 04:35.004
they could turn around and leak info
about the product to Militech.

04:35.587 --> 04:40.467
They'd be a poor fixer
if they weren't a self-serving bastard.

04:40.551 --> 04:44.805
But at the end of the day,
they're only glorified corporate lapdogs.

04:45.431 --> 04:50.769
We'll just remind them
whose hand they eat off of in this city.

04:51.353 --> 04:53.022
How would you go about this?

04:54.773 --> 04:57.818
We tell them
in the only language this city speaks.

05:07.536 --> 05:08.495
Hey…

05:15.002 --> 05:18.130
Take the fixer! Kill the others!

05:20.132 --> 05:21.258
Grenade!

05:21.342 --> 05:22.343
Go! Go!

05:41.403 --> 05:43.030
I was very nearly killed.

05:43.113 --> 05:45.824
What makes you think it was Arasaka?

05:45.908 --> 05:48.660
Do you take me for a fool?
Who else could it have been?

05:48.744 --> 05:52.039
We're not paying
for any additional liabilities.

05:52.122 --> 05:54.416
And corporate immunity
is still off the table.

05:54.500 --> 05:55.667
Are you serious?!

05:55.751 --> 05:59.421
We're already in the red
with your slip-up on the Tanaka case.

05:59.505 --> 06:04.426
With nothing to show for it.
We expect returns on our investments.

06:04.510 --> 06:07.054
Want more resources? Show us results.

06:07.137 --> 06:10.307
And what the hell do you think
I've been chasing?

06:10.390 --> 06:15.687
You're running out of time.
Our patience is running thin.

06:15.771 --> 06:19.191
Arasaka's security
is on higher alert than usual.

06:19.274 --> 06:23.862
Goes to show just how important
the cyberskeleton is to them.

06:23.946 --> 06:25.197
You expect too much.

06:25.280 --> 06:30.369
Don't lecture me on the stakes
with all the money we've invested in this.

06:30.452 --> 06:34.373
Not another enny until you earn it.
We're done here.

06:39.461 --> 06:41.505
Damn corporate brat…

06:51.640 --> 06:54.351
The fixer's made contact.

06:55.144 --> 06:56.478
As I predicted.

06:57.062 --> 06:59.106
What a good little dog.

07:07.406 --> 07:08.740
David?

07:11.201 --> 07:13.620
Oh, my bad.

07:13.704 --> 07:15.330
Did I wake you up?

07:15.414 --> 07:16.832
Can't sleep?

07:16.915 --> 07:18.584
Couldn't shut my brain off.

07:19.209 --> 07:20.210
Oh.

07:20.294 --> 07:21.128
I'll turn it off.

07:21.211 --> 07:22.754
Aren't you watching?

07:22.838 --> 07:24.840
No, I just had it on…

07:24.923 --> 07:25.757
Oh.

07:26.425 --> 07:31.388
250K to the Moon…
Huh, cheaper than I thought.

07:31.472 --> 07:33.390
For a one-way ticket.

07:33.474 --> 07:35.517
Well, yeah.

07:36.727 --> 07:37.895
You remembered…

07:37.978 --> 07:39.021
Huh?

07:39.104 --> 07:41.231
Nothing. I'm going back to bed.

07:41.982 --> 07:43.650
Okay. 'Night.

07:51.825 --> 07:56.038
The world's greatest corporation
conducting illicit business at a diner.

07:56.622 --> 07:59.791
I thought you'd find
the familiarity reassuring.

07:59.875 --> 08:02.294
I won't pick hairs.
I'm here for your answer.

08:02.377 --> 08:07.424
The cyberskeleton project is
a delicate topic even within Arasaka.

08:07.508 --> 08:11.803
It turned problematic when Tanaka
over-consolidated the operational data.

08:11.887 --> 08:14.431
How much does Militech already know?

08:14.515 --> 08:16.350
Information is the blood of my trade.

08:16.433 --> 08:18.936
I'll need some assurances
before I say any more.

08:19.019 --> 08:23.357
We respect that
you're the best man for the job.

08:23.440 --> 08:27.861
We'll gladly provide the compensation
Militech foolishly denied you.

08:27.945 --> 08:30.948
As for the Tanaka mess,
consider your debt settled.

08:31.031 --> 08:32.199
Wonderful.

08:32.282 --> 08:35.577
However, we have some conditions as well.

08:36.495 --> 08:37.454
Let's hear it.

08:37.538 --> 08:42.834
We need to eliminate anyone
who knows about the cyberskeleton.

08:42.918 --> 08:44.503
Done.

08:44.586 --> 08:46.255
And one more thing.

08:46.338 --> 08:47.506
Yes?

08:47.589 --> 08:49.132
After Tanaka died,

08:49.216 --> 08:54.638
there's been a runner interfering
with our recovery on the corrupt data.

08:54.721 --> 08:57.099
Know anything about it?

08:57.808 --> 08:59.059
Not that I can recall.

08:59.142 --> 08:59.977
I see.

09:00.060 --> 09:02.938
We're quite curious about this case.

09:03.021 --> 09:08.735
Even if this were Militech,
I can't even imagine why they'd do this.

09:08.819 --> 09:10.654
From what my sources tell me,

09:10.737 --> 09:15.158
no one else knows about Tanaka's ties
to the cyberskeleton project.

09:15.242 --> 09:16.118
An inside job?

09:16.201 --> 09:21.707
No. It's impossible to move internally
without leaving a trail.

09:21.790 --> 09:27.379
It's more natural to think that
it's a skilled runner from the outside.

09:27.462 --> 09:30.340
Seems to me like a job for a fixer.

09:31.008 --> 09:32.884
Is this an official commission?

09:33.468 --> 09:38.390
One million to take them alive.
Half the price for their head.

09:39.850 --> 09:41.435
I accept.

11:20.909 --> 11:23.245
Take that!

11:24.037 --> 11:25.205
Out of juice!

11:25.288 --> 11:26.748
Gotcha.

11:45.892 --> 11:47.185
What are you doing?!

11:48.145 --> 11:50.105
Ah… My bad.

11:51.523 --> 11:53.066
Later, David.

11:53.150 --> 11:54.151
Yeah…

11:59.614 --> 12:01.199
Falco! Lemme off too!

12:01.283 --> 12:02.325
What?

12:05.287 --> 12:08.039
Well dang,
guess the after-party's just us two.

12:08.123 --> 12:11.042
I've got somewhere to be, too.

12:11.126 --> 12:14.463
That so? Bunch of killjoys,
you, one and all.

12:15.714 --> 12:17.007
David!

12:19.134 --> 12:20.927
No after-party today?

12:21.011 --> 12:23.638
Can't get drunk with those two boomers.

12:23.722 --> 12:26.016
Can't promise I'll be any more fun.

12:26.099 --> 12:27.851
Don't underestimate yourself!

12:28.643 --> 12:30.520
Hey… Wanna take a walk?

12:30.604 --> 12:33.315
Huh? Sure, I guess…

12:33.398 --> 12:34.608
Yes!

12:38.528 --> 12:41.156
So… you doing okay?

12:41.239 --> 12:42.240
What?

12:42.324 --> 12:44.743
What was that today?

12:44.826 --> 12:46.453
What was what?

12:46.536 --> 12:47.787
You know what I mean.

12:48.413 --> 12:49.706
It was nothing.

12:49.789 --> 12:51.833
This isn't the first time it's happened.

12:52.709 --> 12:54.503
You thought I didn't notice?

12:55.504 --> 12:56.630
Whatever.

12:56.713 --> 12:58.757
A girl's intuition, you know?

12:58.840 --> 12:59.841
What girl?

12:59.925 --> 13:01.301
Shut up.

13:03.220 --> 13:07.307
You're the only one I watch
that closely, you know.

13:08.225 --> 13:11.520
Come on, David. What's wrong?

13:12.687 --> 13:13.855
Nothing.

13:13.939 --> 13:15.357
I said cut the bull.

13:15.440 --> 13:17.150
It's got nothing to do with you.

13:17.234 --> 13:21.404
Like hell it doesn't.
I'm putting my life in your hands.

13:22.822 --> 13:24.115
Sorry.

13:26.493 --> 13:28.036
I was thinking…

13:28.620 --> 13:29.454
Yeah?

13:30.080 --> 13:32.415
You should lay off
the implants for a while.

13:32.999 --> 13:35.168
Don't worry. I've got your back!

13:35.835 --> 13:36.795
You?

13:36.878 --> 13:38.547
I'm being serious.

13:39.881 --> 13:43.218
Remember the psycho
that flatlined my brother?

13:43.927 --> 13:45.262
Yeah.

13:45.345 --> 13:49.432
I don't… wanna see you end up like that.

13:51.142 --> 13:51.977
Yeah.

14:24.843 --> 14:27.846
They're still sending runners?

14:59.753 --> 15:00.629
Hm?

15:00.712 --> 15:03.131
Who are you? W-What the…

15:34.579 --> 15:35.413
Wait…

16:18.248 --> 16:19.624
David!

16:26.506 --> 16:28.591
Rise and shine.

16:29.217 --> 16:30.218
Doc…

16:30.301 --> 16:32.554
Symptoms settling down?

16:32.637 --> 16:33.680
Yeah…

16:37.809 --> 16:39.352
When did it start?

16:39.436 --> 16:40.520
What?

16:40.603 --> 16:44.524
Shaky hands, dizziness,
nausea, usual suspects.

16:44.607 --> 16:47.027
A little while ago.

16:47.110 --> 16:49.320
Why didn't you tell me?

16:49.404 --> 16:51.197
Thought it was temporary.

16:51.281 --> 16:54.325
Looks like side-effects
are finally catching up with you.

16:54.409 --> 16:59.456
Of course, it's crazy enough
how you've been fine until now.

16:59.539 --> 17:01.082
Why now?

17:01.166 --> 17:04.878
Lay off the chrome for a while.

17:04.961 --> 17:08.423
You're already one foot
in the psycho zone.

17:08.506 --> 17:11.092
Then gimme stronger meds for it!

17:11.176 --> 17:16.139
Shit. You ain't hearing me.
Or have you already lost your mind?

17:16.222 --> 17:18.975
Ain't no such miracle drug in exist…

17:20.393 --> 17:26.483
Think I came for jokes?
Take my fucking money…

17:26.566 --> 17:28.902
and gimme the fucking meds!

17:28.985 --> 17:30.361
David!

17:39.537 --> 17:45.126
There. Your last prescription. Nine times
standard dosage, good for nine days.

17:45.210 --> 17:49.756
It'll send you straight over the edge
and right to hell.

17:50.423 --> 17:53.510
I'm sorry. I won't let it happen again.

17:53.593 --> 17:54.719
It's fine.

17:54.803 --> 17:59.891
The fact that you need those meds means
you won't be coming back here anymore.

18:01.142 --> 18:04.896
A kid off the block pushing XBDs and now…

18:05.688 --> 18:10.568
Go be a legend or
whatever the fuck you punks do.

18:18.618 --> 18:20.912
Just another tale for the next dreamer…

18:21.412 --> 18:25.333
David! Wait! What was that?

18:25.917 --> 18:27.335
Don't tell the guys.

18:28.128 --> 18:29.337
I don't understand.

18:33.424 --> 18:34.259
Hey!

18:39.722 --> 18:43.226
Your body, your mind…
They have limits, David. You knew that.

18:43.309 --> 18:46.604
Normal meds don't do it for you anymore.

18:46.688 --> 18:48.064
Isn't it time to call quits?

18:49.232 --> 18:53.987
I can't watch you do this to yourself.
Scale back your cyberware…

18:54.654 --> 18:56.114
I can't do that.

18:56.197 --> 18:57.073
Why not?

18:58.116 --> 19:02.328
Mom and Maine…
They all left me something to do.

19:03.329 --> 19:05.331
But I haven't done nothing yet.

19:05.415 --> 19:08.793
But you can't keep going on like this…

19:08.877 --> 19:11.004
I'll be fine.

19:11.087 --> 19:15.550
How could you say that?
Do you really think you're special?

19:16.634 --> 19:21.139
I withstood the Sandevistan.
I'm not normal.

19:22.515 --> 19:28.354
So you're a little more sturdy than
everyone else. But you're still human.

19:31.232 --> 19:32.859
I shot a woman.

19:32.942 --> 19:33.776
Huh?

19:35.111 --> 19:38.156
She was around the same age as my mom.

19:38.907 --> 19:40.658
She also had a son like me.

19:42.994 --> 19:45.622
A harmless bystander. A normal person.

19:47.123 --> 19:50.126
I don't know how many I've killed anymore.

19:51.753 --> 19:54.130
It doesn't even make me pause anymore.

19:55.506 --> 19:59.010
Maybe I really am going crazy.

19:59.636 --> 20:00.553
David…

20:01.471 --> 20:05.225
I ain't normal.
Like you said before, I'm different.

20:05.308 --> 20:06.643
You're not.

20:06.726 --> 20:08.019
I am!

20:08.728 --> 20:10.355
You're not.

20:10.438 --> 20:12.148
You wouldn't understand.

20:13.608 --> 20:17.028
You left the crew after Maine died.

20:17.111 --> 20:18.529
That's because…

20:18.613 --> 20:20.281
I'm not blaming you.

20:20.365 --> 20:21.532
Why not?

20:21.616 --> 20:24.410
You shouldn't have to live this life.

20:24.494 --> 20:27.914
No, David. That's not what I…

20:27.997 --> 20:30.833
Then you'll come back?

20:30.917 --> 20:34.337
Let's go back to the way things were,
working together.

20:38.424 --> 20:41.678
I can't right now.
Wait for me a little while longer.

20:41.761 --> 20:42.595
What for?

20:43.680 --> 20:46.307
There's something I need to do first.

20:46.391 --> 20:48.142
Like what?

20:48.226 --> 20:49.811
I can't say.

20:50.436 --> 20:51.521
Why?

20:51.604 --> 20:52.563
Sorry.

20:53.231 --> 20:55.024
Because you don't trust me.

20:55.733 --> 20:57.026
I'm sorry.

20:58.111 --> 21:01.197
Okay. I'll stop asking you about it.

21:01.281 --> 21:02.115
Okay.

21:03.741 --> 21:07.453
Maybe we should go our separate ways.

21:08.204 --> 21:10.623
No! That's not true David.

21:18.131 --> 21:21.884
I'm sorry, David. I have to go.

21:21.968 --> 21:24.387
Huh? Where?

21:25.847 --> 21:27.223
I have to go…

21:29.309 --> 21:30.768
Okay.

21:30.852 --> 21:32.395
We'll talk when I get home.

21:33.104 --> 21:34.939
Wait for me.

21:49.203 --> 21:51.789
The same ID as the runner from before.

21:52.957 --> 21:54.334
There you are…

22:19.150 --> 22:22.362
Didn't think it would be so easy.

22:26.324 --> 22:29.952
This is our passport into Arasaka.

22:30.036 --> 22:32.330
Excellent job, Kiwi.
